Setting up grid coordinates with D=(0,0), A=(12,0), B=(12,8), C=(0,8), E=(6,0), and P=(0,2), the ball travels at 45° (slope ±1), reflecting off cushions:

- From P(0,2) up-right to (6,8) on the top cushion;
- reflects down-right to (12,2) on the right cushion;
- reflects down-left to (10,0) on the bottom cushion (not a pocket);
- reflects up-left to (2,8) on the top cushion;
- reflects down-left to (0,6) on the left cushion;
- reflects down-right to (6,0) — exactly the middle pocket E.

Thus the ball falls into pocket E.

\boxed{E}
